# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Client-safe, PUBLIC identifiers only — no
# secrets belong in any VITE_ var, because Vite inlines them into the browser
# bundle at build time. Anything here ships to every visitor.
#
# Server-side secrets (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, the oracle and admin
# keypairs) are deliberately NOT listed here. See "Server-side secrets" at the
# bottom for where those actually go.

# --- Shared market feed (Supabase / Lovable Cloud) ---------------------------
# Both values are public. RLS (supabase/migrations/0001_market_state.sql) gives
# this key read-only access to market data and nothing else — it cannot write a
# price or forge a chart point.
#
# NOTE the key name: it is PUBLISHABLE, not ANON. src/integrations/supabase/
# client.ts (generated and owned by Lovable Cloud) reads
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. Setting VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY instead leaves
# the client unconfigured, and the app silently falls back to opening prices
# with a flat chart rather than erroring.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Solana ------------------------------------------------------------------
# devnet | mainnet-beta | localnet. Defaults to devnet when unset, so a missing
# var can never silently point the app at mainnet with real funds — see
# src/lib/solana/chain.ts.
VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet

# Optional. Defaults to the cluster's public RPC. Must name the same cluster as
# VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER — vite.config.ts refuses to build a mismatch.
VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=

# Optional. Defaults to the program id in src/lib/solana/sharps-idl.json.
VITE_PROGRAM_ID=

# --- Server-side secrets (NOT here) ------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  bypasses RLS entirely. Supabase Edge Function
#                            secrets + your shell when seeding. Never in a
#                            VITE_ var, never committed.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL, PROGRAM_ID Edge Function secrets for the indexer (same
#                            values as above, no VITE_ prefix).
# ORACLE_KEYPAIR[_PATH]      signs batch_update_price. Oracle host only.
# ADMIN_KEYPAIR_PATH         initialize_config + create_listing. Local only.
#
# Keep ADMIN and ORACLE as separate keys — the program separates those
# privileges on purpose, and reusing one key collapses that separation back
# into a single point of compromise.

# --- Oracle service (oracle/run.ts) ------------------------------------------
# These belong on the oracle host, not in the app build.
#
# TRADER_RPC_URL       Solana MAINNET RPC the traders are read from. The public
#                      endpoint rate-limits hard; use a dedicated one (Helius,
#                      Triton, QuickNode…) for the full cohort.
# SOLANA_CLUSTER       where the market program lives (devnet / mainnet-beta).
# SOLANA_RPC_URL       that cluster's RPC, if not the public default.
# CYCLE_SECONDS        pause BETWEEN cycles, default 30.
# PUSH_ONCHAIN         "0" to index and publish without signing anything.
# LAUNCH_TS            unix seconds; only trades after this count toward scores.
